      "id": "matins",
      "title": "Matins",
      "sourceHeading": "Matins",
      "pages": [
        545
      ],
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Momentaneum et leve tribulationis nostrae supra modum in sublimitate aeternum gloriae pondus operatur in nobis.",
          "english": "Our momentary and light tribulation worketh in us, beyond measure, an eternal weight of glory on high.",
          "sourcePages": [
            545
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "prepared",
            "preparedFor": "Sacrum Florilegium",
            "sourcePages": [
              545
            ],
            "review": "editorial-review-complete"
          },
          "alignment": "reviewed",
          "id": "matins-b0001",
          "verification": "visual-review"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "℣. Domine, labia mea aperies.",
          "english": "℣. O Lord, Thou shalt open my lips.",
          "sourcePages": [
            545
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "prepared",
            "preparedFor": "Sacrum Florilegium",
            "sourcePages": [
              545
            ],
            "review": "editorial-review-complete",
            "method": "exact-source-memory",
            "memoryId": "05d94e2fa44ca4d5"
          },
          "alignment": "reviewed",
          "id": "matins-b0002",
          "verification": "visual-review"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "℟. Et os meum annuntiabit laudem tuam. Gloria Patri, et Filio, et Spiritui Sancto, Sicut erat in principio, et nunc, et semper, et in saecula saeculorum. Amen.",
          "english": "℟. And my mouth shall proclaim Thy praise. Glory be to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit; as it was in the beginning, is now, and ever shall be, world without end. Amen.",
          "sourcePages": [
            545
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "prepared",
            "preparedFor": "Sacrum Florilegium",
            "sourcePages": [
              545
            ],
            "review": "editorial-review-complete"
          },
          "alignment": "reviewed",
          "id": "matins-b0003",
          "verification": "visual-review"
        },
        {
          "type": "rubric",
          "source": "Hymnus",
          "english": "Hymn",
          "sourcePages": [
            545
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "prepared",
            "preparedFor": "Sacrum Florilegium",
            "sourcePages": [
              545
            ],
            "review": "editorial-review-complete",
            "method": "exact-source-memory",
            "memoryId": "3257d8c1148df2f3"
          },
          "alignment": "reviewed",
          "id": "matins-b0004",
          "verification": "visual-review"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Fortes avete milites, Quorum cruore Japonens, Et purpurascit inclytae Ager ferax Ecclesiae.",
          "english": "Hail, brave soldiers, by whose blood the fertile Japanese field of the renowned Church is crimsoned.",
          "sourcePages": [
            545
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "prepared",
            "preparedFor": "Sacrum Florilegium",
            "sourcePages": [
              545
            ],
            "review": "editorial-review-complete"
          },
          "alignment": "reviewed",
          "id": "matins-b0005",
          "verification": "visual-review"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Vestro hunc rigate sanguine, Terramque cordis aridam. Fecunda fructus proferat, Quos horreis caeli inferat.",
          "english": "Water it with your blood, and the dry earth of our heart. May it, made fruitful, bring forth fruits to gather into heaven’s storehouses.",
          "sourcePages": [
            545
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "prepared",
            "preparedFor": "Sacrum Florilegium",
            "sourcePages": [
              545
            ],
            "review": "editorial-review-complete"
          },
          "alignment": "reviewed",
          "id": "matins-b0006",
          "verification": "visual-review"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Antiphona Justorum animae in manu Dei sunt, et non tanget illos tormentum malitiae: visi sunt oculis insipientium mori: illi autem sunt in pace.",
          "english": "Antiphon. The souls of the righteous are in the hand of God, and the torment of wickedness shall not touch them. In the eyes of the foolish they seemed to die, but they are in peace.",
          "sourcePages": [
            545
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "prepared",
            "preparedFor": "Sacrum Florilegium",
            "sourcePages": [
              545
            ],
            "review": "editorial-review-complete"
          },
          "alignment": "reviewed",
          "id": "matins-b0007",
          "verification": "visual-review"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "℣. Nos autem oportet gloriari in cruce Domini nostri Jesu Christi.",
          "english": "℣. But it behoveth us to glory in the Cross of our Lord Jesus Christ.",
          "sourcePages": [
            545
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "prepared",
            "preparedFor": "Sacrum Florilegium",
            "sourcePages": [
              545
            ],
            "review": "editorial-review-complete",
            "method": "exact-source-memory",
            "memoryId": "199b581454fdecd3"
          },
          "alignment": "reviewed",
          "id": "matins-b0008",
          "verification": "visual-review"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "℟. Per quem nobis mundus crucifixus est, et nos mundo.",
          "english": "℟. Through Whom the world is crucified to us, and we to the world.",
          "sourcePages": [
            545
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "prepared",
            "preparedFor": "Sacrum Florilegium",
            "sourcePages": [
              545
            ],
            "review": "editorial-review-complete",
            "method": "exact-source-memory",
            "memoryId": "a26990c7570af546"
          },
          "alignment": "reviewed",
          "id": "matins-b0009",
          "verification": "visual-review"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Oremus,",
          "english": "Let us pray,",
          "sourcePages": [
            545
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "prepared",
            "preparedFor": "Sacrum Florilegium",
            "sourcePages": [
              545
            ],
            "review": "editorial-review-complete",
            "method": "exact-source-memory",
            "memoryId": "e4264868331a5239"
          },
          "alignment": "reviewed",
          "id": "matins-b0010",
          "verification": "visual-review"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Deus, qui Beatos Martyres tuos Joannem, Paulum, et Jacobum Martyrio gloria decorasti: Concede, quaesumus, ut, quorum gloria coronam in caelis veneramur, eorum fortitudinis exemplum et passionis constantiam imitemur in terris. Per Dominum nostrum, etc.",
          "english": "O God, who hast adorned Thy blessed martyrs John, Paul, and James with the glory of martyrdom, grant, we beseech Thee, that we who venerate their crown of glory in heaven may imitate upon earth their example of courage and steadfastness in suffering. Through our Lord, etc.",
          "sourcePages": [
            545
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "prepared",
            "preparedFor": "Sacrum Florilegium",
            "sourcePages": [
              545
            ],
            "review": "editorial-review-complete"
          },
          "alignment": "reviewed",
          "id": "matins-b0011",
          "verification": "source-reading-pending",
          "editorialNote": "The PDF prints irregular case endings in “Martyrio gloria” and “quorum gloria coronam.” The prepared English provisionally renders the intended crown and glory of martyrdom; the printed Latin is retained."
        }
      ]
    },
