        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Oremus, Omnipotens aeterne Deus, qui servis tuis Paulo, Joanni, et Jacobo in Societatem Filii tui vocatis, Apostolicum studium in Gentium conversionem et Haereticorum reductionem inspirasti; ideoque Martyrii gloria decorasti: concede propitius, ut ipsis, et Passionis Sociis in hoc mundo et consolationis deinde in aeterna beatitudine esse mereamur. Per Dominum nostrum Jesum Christum, qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitate Spiritus Sancti Deus, per omnia saecula saeculorum. Amen.",
          "english": "Let us pray. Almighty and eternal God, who didst inspire Thy servants Paul, John, and James, called into the Society of Thy Son, with apostolic zeal for the conversion of the nations and the return of heretics, and therefore adorn them with the glory of martyrdom, mercifully grant that we may be found worthy to share their suffering in this world and their consolation thereafter in everlasting blessedness. Through Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with Thee in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, for ever and ever. Amen.",
          "sourcePages": [
            547
          ],
          "translation": {
